--   Test Description
--
--   This test is intended to demonstrate the functionality of the transmit 
--   buffer management.  Furthermore, this test is intended to test the GEMs 
--   ability to recover from error, provide access to the buffer descriptors 
--   and the transmit frames in a timely way.
--   
--
--   Functional Coverage
--   � Ensure proper operation of the ownership bit.
--   � Ensure proper operation of the wrap bit.
--   � Ensure proper operation of tx_go (tx enable bit).
--   � Ensure writing of tx status is done properly.
--   � Ensure a tx underrun is dealt with properly by the GEM.
--
--   Detailed Test Description
--
--   1. Initialise the GEM for 10M mode operation.
--   2. Enable transmit.
--   3. Try to transmit a frame that is 32 bytes with no crc (no crc should
--      be appended). 
--      However, the first transmit buffer descriptor read has the used bit set.  
--      Therefore, the GEM should halt transmission of the frame and 
--      the 'used bit read' should be set in the transmit status register. 
--      Also, the 'tx used bit read' should be set in the interrupt status register.
--      The transmit buffer queue pointer should be reset to the original value.
--   4. Try to transmit a multibuffer frame. However, during transmission of 
--      the frame, the final transmit buffer descriptor is read with the used bit 
--      set.  This causes an under-run error to be generated because the dma 
--      cannot keep up with the transmission of the buffer (not enough data in 
--      the fifo). Therefore, the under-run error causes the GEM to transmit 
--      a 32-bit jam sequence until transmission is halted. The transmit 
--      buffer queue pointer should be reset to the original value.
--   5. Try to transmit a multibuffer frame. However, during transmission 
--      of the frame, the final transmit buffer descriptor is read with the 
--      used bit set.  This causes an under-run error to be generated because 
--      the dma cannot keep up with the transmission of the buffer 
--      (not enough data in the fifo). Therefore, the under-run error causes 
--      the GEM to transmit a 32-bit jam sequence until transmission is halted. 
--      The transmit buffer queue pointer should be reset to the original value.
--   6. Transmit a good multibuffer frame. Also check that the no-crc bit
--      is only checked on first buffer in frame.
--   7. Transmit a multibuffer frame. Also, during transmission of the frame, 
--      the final transmit buffer descriptor is read with the wrap bit set. 
--      This should cause the transmit buffer queue pointer to be reset to the 
--      original value for the next buffer descriptor read.
--      Also only the final buffer has the no CRC bit set, therefore no CRC 
--      will be generated on the frame.
--   8. Transmit a multibuffer frame.  Also, during transmission of the frame, 
--      the first, second and third transmit buffer descriptors read have the 
--      wrap bit set. This should cause the transmit buffer queue pointer to be 
--      reset to the original value for the next buffer descriptor read 
--      (excluding the last buffer descriptor read).
--   9. Transmit a multibuffer frame.  Also, during transmission of the frame, 
--      the second and third transmit buffer descriptors read have the wrap 
--      bit set. This should cause the transmit buffer queue pointer to be reset
--      to the original value for the next buffer descriptor read 
--      (excluding the first and last buffer descriptor reads).
--   10.Start transmitting a multibuffer frame. However, during transmission
--      of the frame, a new address is written to the transmit buffer queue pointer.
--      This should have no effect on the transmission of the frame.
--   11.Transmit a multibuffer frame with several small buffers (1 byte).
--      Since the FIFO must be almost filled before the TX will start
--      transmission, this successfully completes.
--   12.Start transmitting a multibuffer frame and provide enough data to
--      ensure that the trigger level is reached to start transmission.
--      Now provides lots of data as single bytes in a buffer.
--      This causes an under-run error to be generated because the dma cannot 
--      keep up with the transmission of the buffers (not enough data in the fifo).
--      Therefore, the under-run error causes the GEM to transmit a 32-bit 
--      jam sequence until transmission is halted. The transmit buffer queue 
--      pointer should be reset to the original value.
--   13.Check status and statistics registers and ensure the above operations 
--      were handled properly.
--   14.Reset the tx_go bit and write a new address to the tx_buffer queue
--      pointer register.  Then tranmsit a normal sized frame.  The tx_buffer 
--      queue pointer should be reset to the new address written to the
--      tx_buffer queue pointer register.
--   15.Check status and statistics registers and ensure the above operations 
--      were handled properly.
--      Note: only compatible with 2 wait state or less in tb_dma.v
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wait_states 3
ten_meg_bit  -- 10Mbit/s operation (2.5Mhz tx_clk and rx_clk, 50MHz Pclk and Hclk)

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      1c ffffff00  -- write address of transmit buffer descriptor in memory
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit 
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00080001  -- write 100M operation on speed pin
apbrd      04 00080001  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register



-- ************************************************************************** --
--   3. Try to transmit a frame that is 32 bytes with no crc (no crc should 
--      be appended). 
--      However, the first transmit buffer descriptor read has the used bit set.  
--      Therefore, the GEM should halt transmission of the frame and 
--      the 'used bit read' should be set in the transmit status register. 
--      Also, the 'tx used bit read' should be set in the interrupt status register.
--      The transmit buffer queue pointer should be reset to the original value.
-- ************************************************************************** --

apbrd      1c ffffff00  "SCENARIO 1 : Used bit read in 1st buffer"
                        -- check transmit queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000208  -- Start the transmission by setting the go bit in network control register

-- descriptor reads for first buffer
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff04 80010020 -- length 32 bytes, ownership bit set
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff00 98765000 -- dma reads pointer of 98765000

-- check interrupt and status
apbrd(int) 24 00000008  "SCENARIO 1 : complete"
                        -- check interrupt status - used bit found
apbwr      24 00000008  -- clear interrupt status
apbrd      14 00000001  -- read transmit status register - used bit found
apbrd      14 00000001  -- check the tx status register has not been cleared
apbwr      14 00000001  -- clear the tx status register
apbrd      14 00000000  -- check the tx status register is now cleared


-- ************************************************************************** --
--   4. Try to transmit a multibuffer frame. However, during transmission of 
--      the frame, the final transmit buffer descriptor is read with the used bit 
--      set.  This causes an under-run error to be generated because the dma 
--      cannot keep up with the transmission of the buffer (not enough data in 
--      the fifo). Therefore, the under-run error causes the GEM to transmit 
--      a 32-bit jam sequence until transmission is halted. The transmit 
--      buffer queue pointer should be reset to the original value.
-- ************************************************************************** --

-- start transmission again by writing TX_GO
apbwr      00 00000208   "SCENARIO 2 : Used bit read in third buffer"
                         -- Start the transmission by setting the go bit in network control register

-- descriptor reads for first buffer
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff04 00010020 -- length 32 bytes, no ownership bit (no CRC)
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff00 98765000 -- dma reads pointer of 98765000
dma_rd 98765000 12345678
dma_rd 98765004 11111111
dma_rd 98765008 22222222
dma_rd 9876500c 33333333
dma_rd 98765010 44444444
dma_rd 98765014 55555555
dma_rd 98765018 66666666
dma_rd 9876501c 77777777



-- descriptor reads for second buffer
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff0c 0001001f -- length 31 bytes, no ownership bit set (no CRC)
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff08 98765100 -- dma reads pointer of 98765000
dma_rd 98765100 88888888
dma_rd 98765104 99999999
dma_rd 98765108 aaaaaaaa
dma_rd 9876510c bbbbbbbb
dma_rd 98765110 cccccccc
dma_rd 98765114 dddddddd
dma_rd 98765118 eeeeeeee
dma_rd 9876511c 00ffffff -- only 31 bytes


-- descriptor reads for third buffer
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff14 8001001e -- length 30 bytes, ownership bit set (no CRC)
dma_rd tx_descr ffffff10 98765200 -- dma reads pointer of 98765000


